LEE-broi"],["a red house","ruĝa domo","ROO-ja DO-mo"],["the cities","la urboj","la OOR-boi"],["one cat, two cats","unu kato, du katoj","OO-noo KA-to doo KA-toi"],["one pen, two pens","unu plumo, du plumoj","OO-noo PLOO-mo doo PLOO-moi"],["a lesson, lessons","leciono, lecionoj","le-TSEE-o-no le-TSEE-o-noi"],["red houses","ruĝaj domoj","ROO-jai DO-moi"]]},{"id":"esti-to-be","title":"Esti: to be","text":["Esti is the only verb \"to be\". It does not change: mi estas, vi estas, li estas, ni estas, ili estas. Past: estis. Future: estos."],"rows":[["I am","mi estas","mee ES-tas"],["you are","vi estas","vee ES-tas"],["he / she is","li / ŝi estas","lee / shee ES-tas"],["we are","ni estas","nee ES-tas"],["they are","ili estas","EE-lee ES-tas"]],"ex":[["I am English","mi estas anglo","mee ES-tas AN-glo"],["he is a doctor","li estas kuracisto","lee ES-tas koo-ra-TSEES-to"],["it is Monday","estas lundo","ES-tas LOON-do"],["we are from Uzbekistan","ni estas el Uzbekio","nee ES-tas el ooz-be-KEE-o"],["they are tall","ili estas altaj","EE-lee ES-tas AL-tai"],["I am at home","mi estas hejme","mee ES-tas HEY-me"],["she is tired","ŝi estas laca","shee ES-tas LA-tsa"],["where are you?","kie vi estas?","KEE-e vee ES-tas"],["we are well","ni fartas bone","nee FAR-tas BO-ne"],["the soup is cold","la supo estas malvarma","la SOO-po ES-tas mal-VAR-ma"]]},{"id":"havi-to-have","title":"Havi: to have","text":["Havi (to have) is regular: mi havas, vi havas, li havas. For hunger, Esperanto has its own verb: malsati."],"rows":[["I have","mi havas","mee HA-vas"],["you have","vi havas","vee HA-vas"],["he / she has","li / ŝi havas","lee / shee HA-vas"],["we have","ni havas","nee HA-vas"],["they have","ili havas","EE-lee HA-vas"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","mi havas fraton","mee HA-vas FRA-ton"],["she has two cats","ŝi havas du katojn","shee HA-vas doo KA-toin"],["we have time","ni havas tempon","nee HA-vas TEM-pon"],["I am hungry","mi malsatas","mee mal-SA-tas"],["they have a car","ili havas aŭton","EE-lee HA-vas OW-ton"],["there is a lesson today","hodiaŭ estas leciono","ho-DEE-ow ES-tas le-TSEE-o-no"],["there is no teacher","ne estas instruisto","ne ES-tas een-stroo-EES-to"],["I have a question","mi havas demandon","mee HA-vas de-MAN-don"]]},{"id":"verbs-present-tense","title":"Verbs: present tense","text":["Every verb has the same ending in the present tense, for every person: -as. Take the infinitive (-i) and change it to -as. Parolas = speak/speaks."],"rows":[["paroli (to speak): mi","mi parolas","mee pa-RO-las"],["paroli: vi","vi parolas","vee pa-RO-las"],["paroli: li","li parolas","lee pa-RO-las"],["paroli: ni","ni parolas","nee pa-RO-las"],["paroli: ili","ili parolas","EE-lee pa-RO-las"]],"ex":[["I speak English","mi parolas la anglan","mee pa-RO-las la AN-glan"],["you eat a lot","vi manĝas multe","vee MAN-jas MOOL-te"],["she lives in Paris","ŝi loĝas en Parizo","shee LO-jas en pa-REE-zo"],["we work every day","ni laboras ĉiutage","nee la-BO-ras chee-oo-TA-ge"],["they drink water","ili trinkas akvon","EE-lee TREEN-kas AK-von"],["I read a book","mi legas libron","mee LE-gas LEE-bron"],["you see the sea","vi vidas la maron","vee VEE-das la MA-ron"],["we hear music","ni aŭdas muzikon","nee OW-das moo-ZEE-kon"]]},{"id":"iri-to-go","title":"Iri: to go","text":["Iri (to go) is regular. To say you are about to do something, use the future: mi manĝos (I will eat). To suggest \"let us\", use ni + -u: ni iru!"],"rows":[["I go","mi iras","mee EE-ras"],["you go","vi iras","vee EE-ras"],["he / she goes","li / ŝi iras","lee / shee EE-ras"],["we go","ni iras","nee EE-ras"],["they go","ili iras","EE-lee EE-ras"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","mi iras al la lernejo","mee EE-ras al la ler-NE-yo"],["where are you going?","kien vi iras?","KEE-en vee EE-ras"],["we are going to eat","ni iros manĝi","nee EE-ros MAN-jee"],["she is going to travel","ŝi vojaĝos","shee vo-YA-jos"],["let us go!","ni iru!","nee EE-roo"],["they go home","ili iras hejmen","EE-lee EE-ras HEY-men"],["I go to the market","mi iras al la bazaro","mee EE-ras al la ba-ZA-ro"],["he goes to Paris","li iras al Parizo","lee EE-ras al pa-REE-zo"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Order: subject, verb, object, as in English. The adjective can come before or after the noun. Word order is flexible, because the -n shows the object."],"rows":[["subject + verb + object","mi manĝas panon","mee MAN-jas PA-non"],["adjective + noun","granda domo","GRAN-da DO-mo"],["add time or place","mi laboras ĉi tie hodiaŭ","mee la-BO-ras chee TEE-e ho-DEE-ow"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","mi manĝas panon","mee MAN-jas PA-non"],["Maria reads a book","Maria legas libron","ma-REE-a LE-gas LEE-bron"],["we live in a big house","ni loĝas en granda domo","nee LO-jas en GRAN-da DO-mo"],["he works here today","li laboras ĉi tie hodiaŭ","lee la-BO-ras chee TEE-e ho-DEE-ow"],["the dog is black","la hundo estas nigra","la HOON-do ES-tas NEE-gra"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"ne\" before the verb. Other negatives: neniu (nobody), nenio (nothing), neniam (never). Always compare with the positive form."],"rows":[["not","ne","ne"],["nobody","neniu","ne-NEE-oo"],["nothing","nenio","ne-NEE-o"],["never","neniam","ne-NEE-am"]],"ex":[["I want","mi volas","mee VO-las"],["I do not want","mi ne volas","mee ne VO-las"],["I speak English","mi parolas la anglan","mee pa-RO-las la AN-glan"],["I do not speak English","mi ne parolas la anglan","mee ne pa-RO-las la AN-glan"],["I like it","ĝi plaĉas al mi","jee PLA-chas al mee"],["I do not like it","ĝi ne plaĉas al mi","jee ne PLA-chas al mee"],["she is here","ŝi estas ĉi tie","shee ES-tas chee TEE-e"],["she is not here","ŝi ne estas ĉi tie","shee ne ES-tas chee TEE-e"],["I have a car","mi havas aŭton","mee HA-vas OW-ton"],["I do not have a car","mi ne havas aŭton","mee ne HA-vas OW-ton"],["I understand","mi komprenas","mee kom-PRE-nas"],["I do not understand","mi ne komprenas","mee ne kom-PRE-nas"],["we are tired","ni estas lacaj","nee ES-tas LA-tsai"],["we are not tired","ni ne estas lacaj","nee ne ES-tas LA-tsai"],["he works on Sundays","li laboras dimanĉe","lee la-BO-ras dee-MAN-che"],["he does not work on Sundays","li ne laboras dimanĉe","lee ne la-BO-ras dee-MAN-che"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Start the sentence with \"ĉu\" to make a yes-or-no question. The rest stays the same."],"rows":[["statement","vi estas laca","vee ES-tas LA-tsa"],["question","ĉu vi estas laca?","choo vee ES-tas LA-tsa"],["answer yes / no","jes / ne","yes / ne"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","ĉu vi parolas la anglan?","choo vee pa-RO-las la AN-glan"],["is she a doctor?","ĉu ŝi estas kuracisto?","choo shee ES-tas koo-ra-TSEES-to"],["do you have a pen?","ĉu vi havas plumon?","choo vee HA-vas PLOO-mon"],["are you tired?","ĉu vi estas laca?","choo vee ES-tas LA-tsa"],["is it far?","ĉu ĝi estas malproksime?","choo jee ES-tas mal-PROK-see-me"],["is the restaurant open?","ĉu la restoracio estas malfermita?","choo la res-to-RA-tsee-o ES-tas mal-fer-MEE-ta"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["All start with ki-: kio (what), kiu (who / which), kie (where), kiam (when), kial (why), kiel (how), kiom (how much), kia (what kind)."],"rows":[["what","kio","KEE-o"],["who","kiu","KEE-oo"],["where","kie","KEE-e"],["when","kiam","KEE-am"],["why","kial","KEE-al"],["how","kiel","KEE-el"],["which","kiu","KEE-oo"],["how much / how many","kiom","KEE-om"]],"ex":[["what is this?","kio estas ĉi tio?","KEE-o ES-tas CHEE TEE-o"],["who is she?","kiu ŝi estas?","KEE-oo shee ES-tas"],["where do you live?","kie vi loĝas?","KEE-e vee LO-jas"],["when is the exam?","kiam estas la ekzameno?","KEE-am ES-tas la ek-za-ME-no"],["why are you late?","kial vi malfruas?","KEE-al vee mal-FROO-as"],["how much is it?","kiom ĝi kostas?","KEE-om jee KOS-tas"],["which book?","kiu libro?","KEE-oo LEE-bro"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":["Add -a to the pronoun: mi, mia (my); vi, via (your); li, lia (his); ŝi, ŝia (her); ni, nia (our); ili, ilia (their). They take -j and -n like adjectives."],"rows":[["my","mia","MEE-a"],["your","via","VEE-a"],["his","lia","LEE-a"],["her","ŝia","SHEE-a"],["our","nia","NEE-a"],["their","ilia","EE-lee-a"]],"ex":[["my house","mia domo","MEE-a DO-mo"],["your friends","viaj amikoj","VEE-ai a-MEE-koi"],["his sister","lia fratino","LEE-a fra-TEE-no"],["our teacher","nia instruisto","NEE-a een-stroo-EES-to"],["their car","ilia aŭto","EE-lee-a OW-to"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Esperanto has no formal \"you\". Use \"vi\" for everybody. Add \"sinjoro\" (sir), \"sinjorino\" (madam), \"bonvolu\" (please) for politeness."],"rows":[["sir","sinjoro","seen-YO-ro"],["madam","sinjorino","seen-yo-REE-no"],["please","bonvolu","bon-VO-loo"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","kiel vi fartas?","KEE-el vee FAR-tas"],["how are you? (formal)","kiel vi fartas, sinjoro?","KEE-el vee FAR-tas seen-YO-ro"],["thank you, sir","dankon, sinjoro","DAN-kon seen-YO-ro"],["excuse me, madam","pardonu, sinjorino","par-DO-noo seen-yo-REE-no"],["please sit down","bonvolu sidiĝi","bon-VO-loo see-DEE-jee"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: change -i to -is. Future: change -i to -os. Conditional: -us. The same for every person."],"rows":[["I worked","mi laboris","mee la-BO-rees"],["you worked","vi laboris","vee la-BO-rees"],["I will work","mi laboros","mee la-BO-ros"],["we will work","ni laboros","nee la-BO-ros"],["I would work","mi laborus","mee la-BO-roos"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","hieraŭ mi laboris","hee-E-row mee la-BO-rees"],["she bought a book","ŝi aĉetis libron","shee a-CHE-tees LEE-bron"],["I will call you tomorrow","mi telefonos al vi morgaŭ","mee te-le-FO-nos al vee MOR-gow"],["we will eat at eight","ni manĝos je la oka","nee MAN-jos ye la O-ka"],["they travelled to Spain","ili vojaĝis al Hispanio","EE-lee vo-YA-jees al hees-pa-NEE-o"],["I went to the market","mi iris al la bazaro","mee EE-rees al la ba-ZA-ro"],["he will come later","li venos poste","lee VE-nos POS-te"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Change -i to -u for a command. It is the same for one person or many: venu! Make it negative with \"ne\": ne venu!"],"rows":[["speak!","parolu!","pa-RO-loo"],["do not speak!","ne parolu!","ne pa-RO-loo"],["come!","venu!","VE-noo"]],"ex":[["come here","venu ĉi tien","VE-noo CHEE TEE-en"],["do not come here","ne venu ĉi tien","ne VE-noo CHEE TEE-en"],["sit down","sidiĝu","see-DEE-joo"],["do not sit down","ne sidiĝu","ne see-DEE-joo"],["be quiet","silentu","see-LEN-too"],["do not be late","ne malfruu","ne mal-FROO-oo"],["open the door","malfermu la pordon","mal-FER-moo la POR-don"],["close the window","fermu la fenestron","FER-moo la fe-NES-tron"],["listen to me","aŭskultu min","ows-KOOL-too meen"],["do not worry","ne maltrankviliĝu","ne mal-trank-vee-LEE-joo"],["speak slowly","parolu malrapide","pa-RO-loo mal-ra-PEE-de"],["wait a moment","atendu momenton","a-TEN-doo mo-MEN-ton"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Povi (can), devi (must), voli (want) are followed by the infinitive: mi povas naĝi. \"Ne rajti\" = not allowed."],"rows":[["I can","mi povas","mee PO-vas"],["I must","mi devas","mee DE-vas"],["I want","mi volas","mee VO-las"]],"ex":[["I can swim","mi povas naĝi","mee PO-vas NA-jee"],["I cannot swim","mi ne povas naĝi","mee ne PO-vas NA-jee"],["can you help me?","ĉu vi povas helpi min?","choo vee PO-vas HEL-pee meen"],["we must go","ni devas iri","nee DE-vas EE-ree"],["we must not go","ni ne rajtas iri","nee ne RAI-tas EE-ree"],["I want to eat","mi volas manĝi","mee VO-las MAN-jee"],["I do not want to eat","mi ne volas manĝi","mee ne VO-las MAN-jee"],["you can come","vi povas veni","vee PO-vas VE-nee"],["you cannot come","vi ne povas veni","vee ne PO-vas VE-nee"],["she wants to study","ŝi volas studi","shee VO-las STOO-dee"],["I must work today","hodiaŭ mi devas labori","ho-DEE-ow mee DE-vas la-BO-ree"],["you must not run","vi ne rajtas kuri","vee ne RAI-tas KOO-ree"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["en = in, sur = on, sub = under, apud = next to, proksime de = near, ĉe = at / by, je = at (time)."],"rows":[["in","en","en"],["on","sur","soor"],["under","sub","soob"],["next to","apud","A-pood"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","la libro estas sur la tablo","la LEE-bro ES-tas soor la TA-blo"],["the cat is under the table","la kato estas sub la tablo","la KA-to ES-tas soob la TA-blo"],["I am at school","mi estas en la lernejo","mee ES-tas en la ler-NE-yo"],["I am at home","mi estas hejme","mee ES-tas HEY-me"],["the shop is next to the bank","la butiko estas apud la banko","la boo-TEE-ko ES-tas A-pood la BAN-ko"],["the park is near the station","la parko estas proksime de la stacidomo","la PAR-ko ES-tas PROK-see-me de la sta-tsee-DO-mo"],["we meet in the morning","ni renkontiĝas matene","nee ren-kon-TEE-jas ma-TE-ne"],["the lesson is at nine","la leciono estas je la naŭa","la le-TSEE-o-no ES-tas ye la NOW-a"],["the key is in the bag","la ŝlosilo estas en la sako","la shlo-SEE-lo ES-tas en la SA-ko"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["pli ... ol = more ... than. plej = the most. malpli = less. The same for every adjective: pli bona (better), plej bona (best)."],"rows":[["bigger than","pli granda ol","plee GRAN-da ol"],["better","pli bona","plee BO-na"],["the biggest","plej granda","play GRAN-da"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","granda, pli granda, plej granda","GRAN-da plee GRAN-da play GRAN-da"],["small, smaller, the smallest","malgranda, pli malgranda, plej malgranda","mal-GRAN-da plee mal-GRAN-da play mal-GRAN-da"],["this is better than that","ĉi tio estas pli bona ol tio","CHEE TEE-o ES-tas plee BO-na ol TEE-o"],["this is worse than that","ĉi tio estas pli malbona ol tio","CHEE TEE-o ES-tas plee mal-BO-na ol TEE-o"],["she is taller than me","ŝi estas pli alta ol mi","shee ES-tas plee AL-ta ol mee"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Taŝkento estas pli granda ol Samarkando","tash-KEN-to ES-tas plee GRAN-da ol sa-mar-KAN-do"],["it is the cheapest","ĝi estas la plej malmultekosta","jee ES-tas la play mal-mool-te-KOS-ta"],["the same as","same kiel","SA-me KEE-el"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","li estas instruisto","lee ES-tas een-stroo-EES-to"],["you (plural) are students","vi estas studentoj","vee ES-tas stoo-DEN-toi"],["I am happy","mi estas feliĉa","mee ES-tas fe-LEE-cha"],["she is at school","ŝi estas en la lernejo","shee ES-tas en la ler-NE-yo"],["you are my friend","vi estas mia amiko","vee ES-tas MEE-a a-MEE-ko"],["it is cold","estas malvarme","ES-tas mal-VAR-me"],["I study English","mi lernas la anglan","mee LER-nas la AN-glan"],["he teaches maths","li instruas matematikon","lee een-STROO-as ma-te-ma-TEE-kon"],["they work every day","ili laboras ĉiutage","EE-lee la-BO-ras chee-oo-TA-ge"],["is this your book?","ĉu ĉi tio estas via libro?","choo CHEE TEE-o ES-tas VEE-a LEE-bro"],["are they here?","ĉu ili estas ĉi tie?","choo EE-lee ES-tas chee TEE-e"],["do you like tea?","ĉu vi ŝatas teon?","choo vee SHA-tas TE-on"],["what time is it?","kioma horo estas?","KEE-o-ma HO-ro ES-tas"],["whose book is this?","kies libro estas ĉi tio?","KEE-es LEE-bro ES-tas CHEE TEE-o"],["how old are you?","kiom aĝa vi estas?","KEE-om A-ja vee ES-tas"],["how do you say it?","kiel oni diras ĝin?","KEE-el O-nee DEE-ras jeen"],["your book (formal)","via libro, sinjoro","VEE-a LEE-bro seen-YO-ro"],["their house","ilia domo","EE-lee-a DO-mo"],["my phone","mia telefono","MEE-a te-le-FO-no"],["excuse me, sir","pardonu, sinjoro","par-DO-noo seen-YO-ro"],["please sit down (formal)","bonvolu sidiĝi","bon-VO-loo see-DEE-jee"],["come here (informal)","venu ĉi tien","VE-noo CHEE TEE-en"],["yesterday I was tired","hieraŭ mi estis laca","hee-E-row mee ES-tees LA-tsa"],["I will study tomorrow","morgaŭ mi studos","MOR-gow mee STOO-dos"],["we went to the park","ni iris al la parko","nee EE-rees al la PAR-ko"]]}],"name":"Esperanto","id":"eo","flag":"eo","note":""}